xnu 0506: prepare and start the aw88261 speaker amplifiers

The pair answered its ID in the 0505 boots. This adds the register path:
each part's fuses, a soft reset, the stock aw882xx_acf.bin Music profile
(device 0 at 0x34, device 1 at 0x35), the fuse-derived 0x50 calibration and
the parked, muted state; the TDM pin function on GPIO121/123/124
(sck/ws/data1) and spksw GPIO52 low.

The live device tree is the authority for the data line. Its
tert_tdm_pinctrl (status ok) is sck GPIO121, ws GPIO123 and dout GPIO124
(function mi2s2_data1); tert_mi2s_pinctrl with GPIO122/mi2s2_data0 is
disabled. The two aw882xx_smartpa nodes are sound-channel 0 and 1 on that
shared dout line. The pad takes the vendor's 8 mA drive and pull-down.

The adsp worker calls mondrian_audio_amp_start() only after the graphs are
started, when the bit clock runs: the pair clears power-down, waits for the
PLL to lock, enables the power stage, restores the feedback enable and
unmutes at the profile's volume. The worker then sends the PCM periods and
powers both down with mondrian_audio_amp_stop().

The 57 register/value pairs of each profile are configuration data read from
the phone's stock firmware file; no vendor driver code is copied.

Measured 2026-11-27: both parts answered 0x2113, both 57-register profiles
read back (0x04=0x73c3 parked, 0x08=0x00f6/0x00f7), and the fuses gave icalk
992/1001 against vcalk 992/994. Both PLLs lock (SYSST 0x0011), both mutes
release at the profile volume (0x1800/0x0800), the PCM write completes with
status 0, VBAT is 3598 mV and PVDD tracks it.

The start's second SYSST check wanted SWS and BSTS; the part reported 0x0011
while still muted and the check aborted. Upstream aw88261 fixed the same
false failure in 2026 ("check sysst fail, reg_val=0x0011"): only PLLS and
CLKS are required before the mute release. This does that, then looks for
SWS|BSTS after the release and logs VBAT and PVDD.

The first data pad was GPIO122 (mi2s2_data0), first tri-stated and then
driven, and it never showed the fill (0.05-0.45 % high over the periods).
That pin is the disabled I2S group's sd0/capture line; the pair listens on
GPIO124 (mi2s2_data1). The mux now uses GPIO124 and the sampler reads it.
The fill is a one-LSB sign square (+1/0xffffffff): inaudible, but the
negative half sets every bit, so the line shows it whatever width the
interface transmits. spksw is sampled as a known-high control.
